      "target": "Let G=(V,E) be a finite simple undirected graph with |V|>=4. Assume (i) deg_G(v)=3 for every v in V; (ii) G is 3-vertex-connected, meaning G-S is connected for every S subset of V with |S|<=2; (iii) G is bipartite; and (iv) G is planar. Prove that G has a Hamiltonian cycle, meaning a simple cycle containing every vertex exactly once, or give one explicit G satisfying (i)-(iv) and rigorously prove it has no Hamiltonian cycle.",
      "title": "Barnette's Hamiltonicity Conjecture"
    },
