      "target": "For a finite simple undirected graph G, let nu(G) be the maximum size of a set of pairwise edge-disjoint triangles, and let tau(G) be the minimum number of edges whose deletion makes G triangle-free. Prove tau(G)<=2 nu(G) for every G, or give an explicit G and rigorously prove tau(G)>2 nu(G).",
      "title": "Tuza's Triangle Packing and Covering Conjecture"
    },
