      "target": "Let X be a finite set and let F be a finite family of distinct subsets of X with at least one nonempty member. Assume A union B belongs to F for every A,B in F. Prove that some x in X belongs to at least |F|/2 members of F, or give explicit finite X and F for which every x belongs to fewer than |F|/2 members, and rigorously verify all conditions.",
      "title": "Frankl's Union-Closed Sets Conjecture"
    },
