      "target": "Let D=(V,A) be a finite loopless simple digraph with n=|V|>=2, no parallel arcs, and minimum out-degree d>=1; antiparallel arcs are allowed and form a directed 2-cycle. Prove that D has a directed cycle of length at most ceil(n/d), or give an explicit D and rigorously prove that its shortest directed cycle has length greater than ceil(n/d).",
      "title": "Caccetta-Haggkvist Directed-Girth Conjecture"
    }
